      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Substance abuse in pain management can undermine treatment compliance, the effectiveness of therapies, and social support and functioning."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIAL",
          "content": "An overview is given regarding pain management for patients on chronic use of opioids and for patients with drug dependence and substance abuse."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Clinical experience as well as relevant documentation demonstrates that management of these patients remains one of the most challenging problems in clinical medicine."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Assessment and treatment plans for this patient group require an understanding of tolerance, physical dependence and drug abuse. It is imperative that the patient's ongoing treatment is planned in a multidisciplinary setting, so as to assure a consistent, structured and shared approach by all caregivers."
        }
      ]},
